Teach libpsl's bundled `config.sub` about Apple's iOS-simulator host triplet.

`build.sh` configures libpsl with `--host=$HOST_TRIPLET --build=$BUILD_TRIPLET`,
and forge builds three iOS slices: `arm64-apple-ios` (device),
`arm64-apple-ios-simulator` and `x86_64-apple-ios-simulator`. autoconf
canonicalises both of those triplets through `build-aux/config.sub` (libpsl
0.21.5 ships the 2022-01-03 vintage) before anything is compiled. For the
simulator name that script produces machine `<cpu>-apple` and OS
`ios-simulator`, then splits the OS on its dash into kernel `ios` and OS
`simulator`. The bare word `simulator` survives the recognised-OS list only by
accident -- it matches the unrelated `sim*` entry meant for bare-metal
simulator targets -- and then hits the block that validates kernel/OS *pairs*,
which has no case for `ios` + `simulator` and falls through to its catch-all:

    Invalid configuration `arm64-apple-ios-simulator': Kernel `ios' not known
    to work with OS `simulator'.

configure aborts there. The device triplet `arm64-apple-ios` and all four
Android triplets canonicalise cleanly, so the symptom is "iOS simulator slices
fail instantly, everything else builds" -- a triplet-parsing problem, not a
compiler or libpsl problem.

The patch adds an empty `ios-simulator)` case to that pairing block, next to
the existing `*-eabi*` entry, declaring the combination valid and leaving it
unnormalised. `arm64-apple-ios-simulator` then canonicalises to
`aarch64-apple-ios-simulator`; no other triplet's handling changes.

Without it the two simulator slices of flet-libpsl fail at configure, and since
flet-libpsl is a host requirement of flet-libcurl, the break propagates down
the whole chain (flet-libcurl, flet-libproj, flet-libgdal, pyproj) on iOS.

The commit that introduced this file (ec8d184, a bulk branch consolidation)
records no rationale; the account above is reconstructed from the diff and
confirmed by running libpsl's own config.sub against forge's triplets, patched
and unpatched.

diff --git a/build-aux/config.sub b/build-aux/config.sub
index dba16e8..215b8e2 100755
--- a/build-aux/config.sub
+++ b/build-aux/config.sub
@@ -1792,6 +1792,8 @@ case $kernel-$os in
 		;;
 	*-eabi* | *-gnueabi*)
 		;;
+	ios-simulator)
+		;;
 	-*)
 		# Blank kernel with real OS is always fine.
 		;;
